  "funFact": "Acorn worms burrow through sand like earthworms, but they are hemichordates — deuterostomes, the same major lineage as sea stars, sea urchins, and vertebrates. This group (Ambulacraria) links hemichordates with echinoderms in the evolutionary tree. Feather worms are polychaete annelids — protostomes that split from deuterostomes over 600 million years ago.",
